# A meadow of pixel sprites on paper: pictures drawn by hand, placed by numbers.
#   ./intent svg examples/art/meadow.intent --style blocks
# A picture is written as rows of characters; its legend says which colour each one stands for.
# The tulips stand where a grid of spots says, and the small flowers fill in between.

The board is 48 wide and 36 high.
The background is light yellow.

A tulip looks like this, where r is crimson, p is hot pink and g is forest green:
    r.r.r
    rrprr
    rrrrr
    .rrr.
    g.g.g
    .ggg.
    ..g..

A daisy looks like this, where w is white and y is gold:
    .w.
    wyw
    .w.

A bird looks like this, where w is white, o is dark orange, k is black and p is pink:
    ..ww...
    .wkwoo.
    ..www..
    .pwwww.
    .wwwwwww
    ..wwwww.
    ...o.o..

Spots have an x (number) and a y (number).
At the start there is a spot for every x from 0 to 4 and every y from 0 to 2.

Draw each spot as a daisy at its x times 10 plus 7 and its y times 11 plus 9.
Draw each spot as a tulip at its x times 10 plus 2 and its y times 11 plus 3.
Draw a bird at 38 and 27.
Write "spring, in sentences" at 3 and 35 in dark olive green.
